      "message": "Thanks for flagging! Checked the preload wiring: PolyGerritIndexHtml.soy injects the same $defaultChangeDetailHex into both \u003clink rel\u003d\"preload\"\u003e and window.DEFAULT_DETAIL_HEXES.changePage, and GrRestApiServiceImpl.getChangeOptionsHex() prefers window.DEFAULT_DETAIL_HEXES.changePage whenever set (only falling back to getChangeOptions() on SPA navigations where no preload occurred). So Old Backend + New Frontend still gets a 100% preload hit without dual preloading, and we will roll out the FE release before the BE release so Old Frontend never receives defaultChangeDetailHex without PARENTS.",
